    "answer": {
      "short": "$m_{AB}=8$, $m_{PQ}=-\\frac18$. Their product is $-1$, so $AB\\perp PQ$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}&=\\frac{12-60}{-1-5}\\\\m_{AB}&=\\frac{-48}{-6}\\\\m_{AB}&=8\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}m_{PQ}&=\\frac{8-10}{23-7}\\\\m_{PQ}&=\\frac{-2}{16}\\\\m_{PQ}&=-\\frac18\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}m_{AB}m_{PQ}&=8\\times\\left(-\\frac18\\right)\\\\m_{AB}m_{PQ}&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nThe product of the gradients is $-1$, so the lines are perpendicular.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
